# SPEC — Magic Cabinet (the product)

> A predictive kitchen cabinet layout engine. Customers measure their kitchen. The layout engine generates buildable cabinet placements. Installers receive build sheets. AI agents query via MCP.

---

## Product

Homeowners and contractors measure kitchen dimensions. The Magic Cabinet engine validates constraints, generates cabinet layouts, assigns materials, and produces installer-facing build sheets. Wrong predictions make the model better. The installer on-site is the final validator.

### Flow 1: Customer measures kitchen

```
Customer measures kitchen with laser tool
  → Creates Room "My Kitchen" → room.state = draft
  → Adds 4 Walls with length and height → wall.state = measured
  → Marks obstacles: windows, doors, range, sink → wall.state = has_obstacles
  → Requests layout: style=modern, budget=standard
  → Layout engine generates cabinet placements
  → Customer reviews, confirms → cabinets.state = confirmed → room.state = locked
```

### Flow 2: Installer receives build sheet

```
Room is locked, all cabinets confirmed, materials assigned
  → Build sheet generated: wall-by-wall cabinet list with positions
  → Material list: quantities, lead times, stock status
  → Installer arrives on site
  → If obstacle missed → reports via app → layout re-plans affected wall only
  → Cabinets installed → cabinet.state = installed
```

### Flow 3: AI agent queries specs (MCP)

```
Developer: "Add 800mm base cabinet option"
  → AI Agent queries MCP: getEntity("Cabinet")
  → Sees width constraint: 150-1200, step 50
  → 800mm is not in the set
  → AI Agent: "Constraint violation: 800mm is not a valid step. Nearest: 750mm or 850mm."
```

---

## Capabilities

### Capability: generate-layout

Given a room with measured walls, place cabinets automatically following design rules.

```yaml
capability: generate-layout
actor: Layout Engine (system)
inputs:
  room_id: string (required)
  style_preference: enum[modern, traditional, transitional, farmhouse] (required)
  budget_tier: enum[economy, standard, premium] (required)
outputs:
  walls: Wall[] (with cabinet placements)
  unfilled_gaps: {wall_id: string, gap_mm: number}[] (spaces too small for standard cabinets)
preconditions:
  - room.state >= measured
  - All walls have length and height
  - At least one material exists per budget tier
postconditions:
  - Every wall has cabinets placed OR is flagged as unfillable
  - Every cabinet has a valid material
  - No obstacles are covered
  - Cabinet-to-cabinet gaps <= 50mm
error_states:
  - room_too_small: room total linear length < 1500mm
  - no_materials: no material matches style + budget
  - impossible_layout: walls have obstacles preventing any valid placement
```

### Capability: re-plan-wall

Re-plan a single wall after installer discovers missed obstacle. Does not affect other walls.

```yaml
capability: re-plan-wall
actor: Layout Engine (system)
inputs:
  wall_id: string (required)
  new_obstacle_id: string (required)
outputs:
  updated_cabinets: Cabinet[]
  removed_cabinets: Cabinet[]
  new_gaps: {gap_mm: number}[]
preconditions:
  - room.state === locked
  - new obstacle does not overlap existing obstacles
postconditions:
  - Affected wall has valid cabinet placement
  - Removed cabinets flagged for reorder if already manufactured
error_states:
  - unfillable_wall: no valid cabinet placement possible with new obstacle
```

---

## Constraints

```yaml
constraint: cabinet-widths-discrete
  type: invariant
  statement: Cabinet widths MUST be from the predefined set in 50mm increments (150, 200, 250, ..., 1200)
  enforcement: strict
  violation_consequence: Layout rejected. No custom widths.

constraint: no-obstacle-overlap
  type: invariant
  statement: No cabinet may overlap any obstacle on its wall. Cabinet position + width must not intersect obstacle position + width.
  enforcement: strict
  violation_consequence: Layout rejected. Physically impossible.

constraint: total-fill
  type: business_rule
  statement: Total cabinet width on a wall MUST <= wall.length. Unfilled space is acceptable but must be reported.
  enforcement: strict
  violation_consequence: Layout rejected. Cabinets cannot extend beyond wall.

constraint: material-availability
  type: business_rule
  statement: Cabinets may use available or backordered materials. Discontinued materials are blocked.
  enforcement: strict
  violation_consequence: Cabinet placement blocked until material reassigned.

constraint: sink-base-position
  type: business_rule
  statement: A sink-base cabinet MUST be placed where a sink obstacle exists on the wall, centered on the obstacle.
  enforcement: soft (warn if violated, allow override)
  violation_consequence: Warning shown. Installer will flag during build.

constraint: measurement-confidence
  type: invariant
  statement: Layout acceptance probability MUST be weighted by measurement method. Laser > tape > photo_estimate > unknown.
  enforcement: soft
  violation_consequence: Layout generated but flagged with confidence warning for photo_estimate or unknown methods.
```

---

## Uncertainty

### Assumptions

```yaml
assumption: Installers can handle gaps <= 50mm with filler strips
  confidence: high
  basis: Industry standard. All cabinet manufacturers produce filler strips in 25mm increments.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Survey 50 installers: "Can you handle 50mm gap with standard filler?"
  if_wrong: Maximum allowable gap drops to 25mm. Layout engine must fit cabinets more tightly.

assumption: Users measure room dimensions within +/- 5mm accuracy
  confidence: medium
  basis: Consumer laser measures are common. No data on our userbase yet.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Compare first 100 submitted measurements to on-site installer verification.
  if_wrong: Add 10mm tolerance buffer to all constraints. Or require professional measurement.

assumption: Material lead times from supplier are accurate within +/- 2 days
  confidence: low
  basis: Supplier claims 14-day lead time. No order history to verify.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Track actual delivery dates for first 50 orders.
  if_wrong: Add buffer to project timeline. Flag supplier as unreliable. Source backup material.

assumption: Customers understand the difference between base/wall/tall cabinet types
  confidence: speculative
  basis: None. We haven't tested customer comprehension.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Show 10 customers a layout. Ask them to identify base vs wall cabinets.
  if_wrong: Add visual labels to layout view. Remove jargon from customer-facing output.
```

### Outcome Sets (Probabilistic Branches)

```yaml
outcome_set: installer-revision-rate
  description: Probability that an installer must modify a layout on-site
  branches:
    no_changes: 0.40
    minor_filler_adjustment: 0.35
    cabinet_resized: 0.15
    layout_rejected: 0.10
  basis: Industry benchmark from NKBA installer survey
  sensitivity: Most affected by measurement accuracy assumption. If measurement error >5mm, layout_rejected doubles.

outcome_set: material-delay-impact
  description: How material backorders affect project completion
  branches:
    on_time: 0.70
    delayed_1_week: 0.15
    delayed_2_weeks: 0.10
    delayed_4_plus_weeks: 0.05
  basis: Supplier SLA data, adjusted for industry trends
  sensitivity: If in-stock rate drops below 85%, on_time drops to 0.40.

outcome_set: first-layout-acceptance
  description: Will the customer accept the first auto-generated layout?
  branches:
    accept_as_is: 0.25
    accept_with_minor_changes: 0.45
    reject_wants_redesign: 0.20
    reject_switches_to_competitor: 0.10
  basis: Competitor benchmarks (IKEA planner: 55% first-acceptance, ProKitchen: 70%)
  sensitivity: Most affected by style-preference accuracy.
```

---

## Failure Modes

```yaml
failure: wall-measurement-wrong
  description: Customer submits measurements off by >50mm
  cause: Using tape measure instead of laser, measuring to trim instead of drywall, transposing digits
  probability: 0.15 (per project)
  impact: high
  detection: Installer reports discrepancy at site visit. Layout validation doesn't catch this (measurement IS the input).
  recovery: Re-plan layout with corrected measurements. Cabinet order may need revision.
  prevention: Require photo upload of laser measure reading. Add "measure twice" prompt. Offer professional measurement.

failure: material-discontinued-mid-project
  description: Material becomes discontinued after layout is locked
  cause: Supplier discontinues SKU without notice
  probability: 0.01 (per material per month)
  impact: high
  detection: Weekly supplier catalog sync. Layout engine flags affected cabinets.
  recovery: Suggest nearest-match alternative material. Auto-reassign if customer approves.
  prevention: Prefer materials with >2 year track record. Flag materials <6 months old as "new — risk of discontinuation."

failure: obstacle-missed
  description: Installer finds an obstacle not in the original measurements
  cause: Customer missed outlet, pipe behind drywall, appliance dimensions wrong
  probability: 0.20 (per project)
  impact: medium
  detection: Installer reports on site. Must re-plan affected wall.
  recovery: Installer marks new obstacle in app. Layout engine re-generates for affected wall only.
  prevention: Checklist of common hidden obstacles. Require photo of each wall before layout lock.
```

### Edge Cases

```yaml
edge_case: corner-cabinet-on-both-walls
  description: Two corner cabinets placed where walls meet — they conflict for the corner space
  expected_behavior: Corner space allocated to one cabinet. Second cabinet starts after corner depth.
  test: Place corner cabinet on wall A. Place second corner cabinet on adjacent wall B. Verify no overlap.

edge_case: window-height-conflict
  description: Wall cabinet placed where window exists — cabinet bottom is below window top
  expected_behavior: Cabinet blocked. Windows occupy full vertical space from sill to top of wall.
  test: Place wall cabinet at position overlapping window. Verify rejection.

edge_case: zero-length-wall
  description: Room has wall with length 0mm (data entry error or genuinely no wall)
  expected_behavior: Wall rejected at validation. Must have length > 0.
  test: Submit room with wall length 0. Verify validation error.

edge_case: all-discontinued-materials
  description: All materials in the system are discontinued. No valid material exists for cabinet assignment.
  expected_behavior: Layout generation fails with clear error. Admin must add materials.
  test: Set all materials to discontinued. Try to generate layout. Verify error message.
```

---

## Scenarios

### Scenario: first-time-user-measures-kitchen

New user measures their L-shaped kitchen and submits for layout.

```
Initial: Room is draft, no walls, no measurements

Steps:
  1. User creates Room "My Kitchen" → room.state = draft
  2. User adds Wall "North" (laser-measured, 3600mm) → wall.state = measured
  3. User adds Wall "East" (laser-measured, 2400mm) → wall.state = measured
  4. User adds Obstacle "Sink Window" on North at 800mm, width 1200mm → wall.state = has_obstacles
  5. User adds Obstacle "Range" on East at 600mm, width 900mm → wall.state = has_obstacles
  6. User requests layout: style=modern, budget=standard
  7. Engine places: sink-base at North[200mm], base cabinets flanking window, corner at east junction,
     base cabinets left of range, tall pantry right of range

Predicted outcome: Valid layout with 85% wall coverage. 50mm filler gap on North, 100mm on East. 8-10 cabinets.
Failure conditions: Layout rejected due to obstacle placement. Total fill < 60%. Corner conflict.
```

### Scenario: material-backorder-during-project

Material goes backordered after layout is locked.

```
Initial: Room locked, all cabinets assigned "white-shaker-oak", project scheduled for 14-day install

Steps:
  1. event material.backordered fires for "white-shaker-oak" with new lead time 28 days
  2. All cabinets using this material flagged
  3. Project timeline extended by 14 days (28 - original 14)
  4. Customer notified of delay
  5. Option A: customer accepts delay → project rescheduled
  6. Option B: customer switches to "white-shaker-maple" (lead time 7 days) → material reassigned

Predicted outcome: 60% accept delay. 40% switch materials.
Failure conditions: No alternative material in same style/price tier. Customer cancels.
```

### Scenario: installer-finds-missed-obstacle

Installer discovers a pipe not in original measurements.

```
Initial: Room locked, all cabinets ordered, installer on site

Steps:
  1. Installer discovers 150mm pipe at 2400mm on North wall
  2. Installer reports obstacle via app → new Obstacle created, wall.state = has_obstacles
  3. Layout engine re-runs for affected wall only
  4. Cabinet at 2300-2900mm conflicts with pipe at 2400-2550mm
  5. Engine removes conflicting cabinet, fills remaining space with smaller cabinets if possible
  6. If gap > 300mm after re-plan, installer gets authorization to use filler

Predicted outcome: 70% resolved same-day with filler. 25% require new cabinet order (1-2 week delay). 5% full wall re-plan.
Failure conditions: Multiple missed obstacles on same wall. No valid replacement cabinet widths available.
```

